WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.710
The Strait of Hormuz: a narrow
route out of the Persian Gulf.

2
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:10.250
In 2024, about 20 million barrels
of oil passed through it a day.

3
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.610
That was about 20 per cent of world
petroleum liquids consumption.

4
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.670
The Middle East produced 31 per
cent of the world's oil that year,

5
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.330
but used only 9.5 per cent.

6
00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.170
So why can no great power, old or rising,

7
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.340
afford to ignore this region?

8
00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:31.070
In this mission, you'll
trace where Hormuz oil goes,

9
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.690
and which powers depend on it most.

10
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:39.570
Then you'll judge, power by power, what
matters most in the region, and why.

11
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:44.200
Your mission: explain why no great
power can ignore the Middle East.
